# AGENT.md — src/presentation/

The outermost layer. Converts HTTP requests into application service calls
and returns HTTP responses.

## What lives here

- `<module>/controller.ts` — Express controllers. Receives `Request` and
  `Response`, calls the application service, and returns JSON.
- `<module>/routes.ts` — exports a function that returns an Express `Router`.
  Defines method, path, optional validation middleware, and controller handler.

## Rules

1. Controllers call application services, never repositories.
2. Every controller catches errors and returns appropriate HTTP responses.
3. Routes are defined as functions (not plain routers) so the controller
   instance can be injected during wiring in `app.ts`.
4. Validation (express-validator chains, Zod schemas) is applied as middleware
   before the controller handler.
5. Controllers use `res.status(code).json(data)`.
6. When adding a new module, mount its routes in `src/app.ts` using
   `app.use('/path', moduleRoutes(controller))`.
